      "title": "Transparent sprite RGB contaminated a straight RGBA atlas crossfade",
      "source_of_finding": "The independent stage judge identified the V8 rendered artifact and the root agent repaired it before this final review.",
      "reviewed_repair_location": "src/scene-assets/effects.scene-asset.ts:78-81",
      "reviewed_equation": "density=mix(first.a,next.a,evolution);radiance=mix(first.rgb*first.a,next.rgb*next.a,evolution)/max(density,.0001);sprite=vec4(radiance,density)",
      "correctness_reason": "A zero-alpha source contributes zero numerator and zero density, so its hidden RGB cannot tint the other sprite during crossfade. The final output remains straight alpha for the material blending path. Division is bounded; the .0001 guard is below the .003 final-alpha discard threshold after opacity factors.",
      "verification_limit": "The equation and bounds were reviewed directly in the actual source. The independent CPU harness does not execute GLSL; final GPU appearance remains the stage/temporal judges scope."
    }
